%% Module 6: Multi-Agent Orchestration — LangGraph State Machine
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Retriever

    Retriever: Retriever Node
    Retriever: calls Module 1+2 pipeline
    Retriever --> Analyst

    Analyst: Analyst Node
    Analyst: drafts answer, flags gaps in confidence
    Analyst --> Reviewer

    Reviewer: Reviewer Node
    Reviewer: runs NLI check from Module 4
    Reviewer --> Decision

    state Decision <<choice>>
    Decision --> Analyst: FAIL, revision_count < 1 — revise with feedback
    Decision --> HumanInterrupt: FAIL, revision_count >= 1
    Decision --> End: PASS

    HumanInterrupt: interrupt() pauses execution,\nstate persisted via checkpointer
    state HumanChoice <<choice>>
    HumanInterrupt --> HumanChoice: human responds
    HumanChoice --> End: approved
    HumanChoice --> Blocked: rejected

    Blocked: Response blocked, logged, not delivered
    Blocked --> [*]
    End --> [*]

    note right of HumanInterrupt
        Checkpointer (MemorySaver) persists
        full state at every node — enables
        crash recovery and audit of exact
        execution path per query
    end note

    note right of Analyst
        revision_count capped at 1 to bound
        latency/cost — unbounded loops are
        a real production risk
    end note
